 ('china', 'EV18', 'Its spokesman, that Monday, in NBC\'s account: "the so-called Chinese spy allegation is unsubstantiated. It is nothing but smears against China". The ministry\'s transcript of that day\'s press conference has him asked, by AFP and NBC, to comment on the board\'s inquiry and Huang\'s acknowledgment of an affair, and answer: "We responded to that last week", and the allegation "is purely unsubstantiated and directed at smearing China" (The National quotes an official of the ministry in "a video address on Monday": "It is nothing but smears against China"); asked that day how China would respond to tighter curbs on chips: "China\'s position on the U.S. export of chips to China is consistent. For anything specific, I\'d refer you to competent authorities"',
  ['art-own-fmprc-1109', 'art-own-fmprc-1109', 'nbc-1108-investigation', 'art-own-fmprc-1109', 'art-own-fmprc-1109', 'art-own-fmprc-1109', 'sw-thenationalnewscom-02'],
  ['How will China respond if the U.S. pushes for tighter tech curbs, including on chips', "China's position on the U.S. export of chips to China is consistent", 'It is nothing but smears against China', 'Can the Chinese foreign ministry comment on this? (Similar question from NBC)', 'We responded to that last week.', 'allegation is purely unsubstantiated and directed at smearing China', "an official with the country's Foreign Ministry said during a video address on Monday"]),
