 ('Anthropic', 'Treasury Secretary Bessent', 'context', 'In an interview from Beijing on May 14, 2026 (CNBC\'s own page: "Following is the unofficial transcript of a CNBC interview"), he said of "all three of the leading companies, Anthropic, OpenAI and Google/Gemini": "all three of the big players have been very good partners with the U.S. government because what we don\'t want to do is stifle innovation", and: "Everything has been voluntary on the, by the companies, and they have been very good partners with the U.S. government"; of its model he said: "We saw a step function jump with Anthropic Mythos". Asked whether there would be a resolution of "supply chain issues with Anthropic" (the president\'s order of February 2026 is on the company\'s line with him), he answered: "I\'m not going to speak for the Department of War. I would isolate their issue with Anthropic. Anthropic has been very engaged with the White House, with Treasury in terms of Mythos and, you know, all their new releases"; and: "the U.S. government has begun consulting with the firms". Reuters that day, in a copy The Business Standard carries: "Government officials have raised alarms about non-state, criminal or terrorist organizations exploiting Mythos to disrupt markets and the global financial system". Reuters, as the International Business Times relays it on Nov 17, 2026, after naming both companies\' limits on the use of their output to train rival models: he "also warned in July that Chinese companies engaging in covert, industrial-scale distillation activities involving intellectual property theft could face sanctions or placement on the US Entity List"; the relay says the technique "is not inherently illegal", and does not say that either company asked for the warning', ['ms-g17-x9-versantmedia-792001', 'ms-g17-x9-versantmedia-792001', 'ms-g17-x9-versantmedia-792001', 'ms-g17-x9-versantmedia-792001', 'ms-g17-x9-versantmedia-792001', 'ms-n18-ibtimes-a2b692', 'ms-n18-ibtimes-a2b692', 'ms-n18-ibtimes-a2b692', 'ms-g17-x9-versantmedia-792001', 'ms-g17-x9-tbsnews-271e10', 'ms-g17-x9-versantmedia-792001'], ['Following is the unofficial transcript of a CNBC interview with U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent on CNBC’s “Squawk Box” (M-F, 6AM-9AM ET) today, Thursday, May 14.', 'all three of the leading companies, Anthropic, OpenAI and Google/Gemini, their large language models are increasing in power very quickly.', "all three of the big players have been very good partners with the U.S. government because what we don't want to do is stifle innovation.", 'Everything has been voluntary on the, by the companies, and they have been very good partners with the U.S. government.', "the U.S. government has begun consulting with the firms. And again, we don't want to stifle innovation. We're just consulting with them. They've been very good partners.", 'OpenAI restricts certain uses of its model outputs to develop competing AI systems, subject to exceptions. Anthropic also imposes restrictions on using its services to train competing models without permission.', 'Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent also warned in July that Chinese companies engaging in covert, industrial-scale distillation activities involving intellectual property theft could face sanctions or placement on the US Entity List.', 'The technique itself is widely used in artificial intelligence development and is not inherently illegal.', "supply chain issues with Anthropic? Will that be handled? What can you tell us? BESSENT: Again, I'm not going to speak for the Department of War. I would isolate their issue with Anthropic. Anthropic has been very engaged with the White House, with Treasury in terms of Mythos and, you know, all their new releases.", 'Government officials have raised alarms about non-state, criminal or terrorist organizations exploiting Mythos to disrupt markets and the global financial system.', 'We saw a step function jump with Anthropic Mythos.']),
