 ('Anthropic', 'Sen. Tim Scott', 'context', 'An essay titled "Inference as Contraband" (its page is dated June 27, 2026) reports a letter to the committee he chairs: "In a letter dated June 10, 2026, submitted to U.S. Senate Banking Committee Chair Tim Scott and Ranking Member Elizabeth Warren, Anthropic documented the largest known distillation campaign ever recorded against its systems", by "operators affiliated with Alibaba’s Qwen AI lab"; the essay says the letter was "reviewed and reported across multiple outlets" and that distillation "is not illegal in all contexts". Business Standard (June 26, 2026) on the same charge: "According to a Reuters report, Anthropic alleged that operators linked to Alibaba conducted the campaign between April 22 and June 5, 2026, creating nearly 25,000 fraudulent Claude accounts and generating more than 28.8 million interactions with the chatbot"; "Alibaba has denied wrongdoing and the allegations have not been independently verified", stating, the paper writes, "that it does not use outputs from proprietary AI models to train its own models and that its AI development complies with applicable intellectual property laws"; and it places the Commerce Department\'s restrictions on two of the company\'s models (on the company\'s own line) on "June 12, two days after the company sent its letter to US lawmakers". The letter itself is not among the saved pages. The same letter is on the company\'s line with Sen. Warren, the ranking member. Saved only in a version changed after its first day, so a passage from it may be newer than that day: the essay\'s page of June 27, 2026 (changed July 2, 2026)', ['ms-sg2-change-b536df', 'ms-sg2-change-b536df', 'ms-sg2-change-b536df', 'ms-sg2-change-b536df', 'ms-sg2-change-b536df', 'art-bs-alibaba', 'art-bs-alibaba', 'art-bs-alibaba', 'art-bs-alibaba', 'art-bs-alibaba'], ['Inference as Contraband', 'In a letter dated June 10, 2026, submitted to U.S. Senate Banking Committee Chair Tim Scott and Ranking Member Elizabeth Warren, Anthropic documented the largest known distillation campaign ever recorded against its systems. According to the letter, reviewed and reported across multiple outlets , operators affiliated with Alibaba’s Qwen AI lab used approximately 25,000 fraudulent accounts and commercial proxy services to generate 28.8 million interactions with Claude between April 22 and June 5, 2026.', 'Distillation, training a less capable model on the outputs of a more advanced system, is not illegal in all contexts.', 'PUBLISHED: 2026-06-27T22:31:11+00:00', 'MODIFIED: 2026-07-02T11:59:25.971Z', 'PUBLISHED: 2026-06-26T15:10:46+05:30', 'According to a Reuters report, Anthropic alleged that operators linked to Alibaba conducted the campaign between April 22 and June 5, 2026, creating nearly 25,000 fraudulent Claude accounts and generating more than 28.8 million interactions with the chatbot.', 'Alibaba has denied wrongdoing and the allegations have not been independently verified.', 'Alibaba has denied the allegations, stating that it does not use outputs from proprietary AI models to train its own models and that its AI development complies with applicable intellectual property laws.', "The issue gained further significance after the US Commerce Department imposed restrictions on Anthropic's latest Mythos and Fable models on June 12, two days after the company sent its letter to US lawmakers."]),
